{"decision":"REJECT","issues":[{"issue_id":"I2-004-LOGIC-001","category":"SOURCE_BACKED_LOGIC_ERROR","source_clause":"I2.1.2.2","source_excerpt":"I2.1.2.2 The ship displacement DUI is the displacement, in kt, of the ship corresponding to the
            upper ice waterline (UIWL). Where multiple waterlines are used for determining the UIWL, the
            displacement is to be determined from the waterline corresponding to the greatest
            displacement.","candidate_excerpt":"                FILTER EXISTS {
                    $this nltl:hasUpperIceWaterlineCase ?case .
                    ?case nltl:waterlineCaseDisplacement ?caseQuantity .
                    ?caseQuantity qudt:numericValue ?caseValue ;
                                  qudt:unit unit:KiloTON_Metric .
                    FILTER (?caseValue > ?upperValue)
                }","insertion_context":null,"reason":"The constraint reports a violation only when a case displacement is greater than DUI. Consequently, a DUI numerically greater than every waterline-case displacement satisfies this query, although it is not the displacement corresponding to the waterline with the greatest displacement. The source requires selection of the greatest displacement, which requires equality with the maximum, not merely absence of a greater case.","expected":"DUI must be numerically equal, in metric kilotonnes, to the greatest displacement among the waterlines used to determine the UIWL.","suggestion":"Replace the one-sided greater-than test with a numeric-equality-to-maximum check, while retaining the declared metric-kiloton unit and decimal quantity paths.","evidence_excerpt":"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineDisplacement> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#recommendedUnit> <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloTON_Metric> .","change_id":null,"property":"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineDisplacement","proposed_unit":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloTON_Metric","proposed_datatype":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal","proposed_path":["https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineDisplacement","https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasUpperIceWaterlineCase","https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#waterlineCaseDisplacement"]},{"issue_id":"I2-004-CONTEXT-001","category":"UNRESOLVED_CONTEXT","source_clause":"I2.1.2.2","source_excerpt":"Where multiple waterlines are used for determining the UIWL, the
            displacement is to be determined from the waterline corresponding to the greatest
            displacement.","candidate_excerpt":"    sh:property [
        a sh:PropertyShape ;
        sh:path nltl:hasUpperIceWaterlineCase ;
        sh:minCount 1 ;
        sh:node nltl:I2_004_UpperIceWaterlineCaseShape ;
        sh:severity sh:Violation ;
        sh:message "Each admitted ship must have at least one upper ice waterline case." ;
    ]","insertion_context":null,"reason":"The supplied schema maps hasUpperIceWaterlineCase to upperIceWaterlineCase, but it does not explicitly establish that every waterline used to determine the UIWL is represented by one of these cases. The candidate therefore cannot be confirmed to compute the greatest displacement over the complete source-relevant set; this is a material representation-adequacy question distinct from the confirmed one-sided comparison error.","expected":"The represented case collection must be established as the complete set of waterlines used for determining the UIWL before the greatest displacement is selected.","suggestion":"Provide or bind an explicit completeness convention for hasUpperIceWaterlineCase, or add a supplied schema path/constraint that establishes the case collection is exhaustive. Do not infer completeness from the RDFS domain/range alone.","evidence_excerpt":"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasUpperIceWaterlineCase> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineCase> .","change_id":null,"property":"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasUpperIceWaterlineCase","proposed_unit":null,"proposed_datatype":null,"proposed_path":["https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasUpperIceWaterlineCase","https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#waterlineCaseDisplacement"]}],"change_assessments":[],"reconciliations":[],"unchecked":[{"scope":"aa7a4df3cc909127170fa72b3879ac21512fb45065a8e41b8fecdbf15060caca","material":false,"reason":"The omitted passage is outside the supplied I2.1.2.2 text needed to identify the greatest-displacement obligation; the exact clause is present. It may affect broader UR I2 review but was not assessed here."},{"scope":"fb42052bcee201b71dea09ac424e8f3157fdf41f16080fc68776c6bd1a4f5bf4","material":false,"reason":"The omitted passage is outside the supplied I2.1.2.2 text needed for this review."},{"scope":"4f2104b852857e63498fdeb8d7b9047cbcd5988fb783ff134a89a1aa4fda61d4","material":false,"reason":"The omitted introductory passages are not needed to assess the supplied I2.1.2.2 displacement-selection clause."},{"scope":"430aaaa772843afc07a12ff9d2269fb81f288142f6c1eed76f59fb0658f46a3e","material":false,"reason":"The omitted passage is outside the supplied requirement clause and no dependency on it is asserted by this candidate."},{"scope":"25867fdf103c32cdbf9a29aecddb5b52617d8b305af51697261e4ae1b6d364dc","material":false,"reason":"The omitted passage is outside the supplied I2.1.2.2 clause; applicability is caller-admitted for this synthetic representation scope."},{"scope":"7af439e2a51193e41a8a56100e56dc9829ad0a1980e549838a9747fe453df9bc","material":false,"reason":"UR F0 is not cited by the supplied requirement or candidate and is outside this clause review."},{"scope":"eeb8981c183fafd8c40cbd6a5fc4104958da9c00f52c3423b3e0118c744dfb6d","material":false,"reason":"The omitted later I2 passage is outside I2.1.2.2 and is not used by the candidate's displacement logic."},{"scope":"e90a8fba9b5fcb5f220863c83c674148b25236119e5825a39afc060c4d6d4296","material":false,"reason":"UR I3 is not cited by the supplied requirement and is outside this representation review."},{"scope":"ba722b8757492b33a461e0c0526364ebd750fe05ca75c3ebd243e0e81a5ae7bd","material":false,"reason":"PR 29 concerns construction-date interpretation and is outside the caller-admitted synthetic scope and I2.1.2.2 displacement condition."},{"scope":"7da24d2967aa5f440f81c2e4fd63e38eec0afb9bf535957c50d7814b19d41798","material":false,"reason":"The supplied candidate retains the applicability text and caller admission supplies the synthetic population context; the omitted UR I1 passage was not needed to identify the I2.1.2.2 numeric obligation."},{"scope":"SPARQL standalone execution context","material":false,"reason":"Static warnings report an unresolved standalone translation environment for the declared nltl prefix, but the candidate includes explicit nltl, qudt, unit, rdf, rdfs and sh declarations. Runtime SHACL execution was not independently verified."}]}

